{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,3]],"date-time":"2025-12-03T20:37:07Z","timestamp":1764794227090},"reference-count":33,"publisher":"World Scientific Pub Co Pte Lt","issue":"17","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Int. J. Mod. Phys. A"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2021,6,20]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> A quark\u2013antiquark effective model is studied in a toroidal topology at finite temperature. The model is described by a Schr\u00f6dinger equation with linear potential which is embedded in a torus. The following aspects are analyzed: (i) the nonclassicality structure using the Wigner function formalism; (ii) finite temperature and size-effects are studied by a generalization of Thermofield Dynamics written in phase space; (iii) in order to include the spin of the quark, Pauli-like Schr\u00f6dinger equation is used; (iv) analysis of the size-effect is considered to observe the fluctuation in the ground state. The size effect goes to zero at zero, finite and high temperatures. The results emphasize that the spin is a central aspect for this quark\u2013antiquark effective model. <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1142\/s0217751x21501219","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,6,5]],"date-time":"2021-06-05T02:58:35Z","timestamp":1622861915000},"page":"2150121","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":5,"title":["Size-effect at finite temperature in a quark\u2013antiquark effective model in phase space"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"36","author":[{"given":"G. X. A.","family":"Petronilo","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Instituto de F\u00edsica, Universidade de Bras\u00edlia, 70910-900, Bras\u00edlia, DF, Brazil"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"R. G. G.","family":"Amorim","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculdade Gama, Universidade de Bras\u00edlia, Setor Leste (Gama), 72444-240 B